      "name": {
        "name": "Exportin-1/5",
        "short": "XPO1/5"
      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "<p>This entry includes exportin-1/5 from eukaryotes.</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        },
        {
          "text": "<p>Exportin-1,  also known as CRM1, is a nuclear export receptor that have been shown to be involved in U3 snoRNA transport from Cajal bodies to nucleoli [[cite:PUB00097970]]. It also controls the composition of many nucleoplasmic complexes [[cite:PUB00097969]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        },
        {
          "text": "<p>Exportin-5 mediates the nuclear export of proteins bearing a double-stranded RNA binding domain (dsRBD) and double-stranded RNAs (cargos) [[cite:PUB00090426]]. Exportin-5 yeast homologue, also known as Msn5, is involved in nuclear import of replication protein A and export of Far1 and transcription factors Swi5, Swi6, Msn2, and Pho4 [[cite:PUB00090428], [cite:PUB00090429], [cite:PUB00090430]]. Its Arabidopsis homologue, HASTY 1, is involved in the nuclear export of microRNAs (miRNAs) [[cite:PUB00090433]].</p>",
          "llm": false,
          "checked": false,
          "updated": false
        }
      ],
